  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intensified Malaria control in high burden provinces towards falciparum eliminations - Iran (Islamic Republic) (01-Apr-2014-30-Sep-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Iran (Islamic Republic), Malaria, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Iran)This program has the following goals: To eliminate local transmission of falciparum malaria by 2015 in target districts.  To prevent malaria deaths in target districts.  To reduce local malaria transmission by 80% by end of 2015 compared to 2009 in target areas. The objectives of this program are: Objective 1: Treatment of all malaria cases according to the National Malaria Treatment Guidelines on the basis of parasitological confirmation of diagnosis.  Objective 2: Protection of at least 90% of at risk people in target districts by vector control measures based on IVM approach.  Objective 3: Prevention of malaria epidemics and re-introduction of malaria falciparum transmission.  Objective 4: The target districts will have strengthened health system and supportive inter-sectoral and community partnership on National Malaria Elimination Programme</narrative>
  </description>
